# Native SEO (no SEO plugins)

You are implementing SEO in this Sage theme only. **Do not install Yoast, Rank Math, SEOPress, AIOSEO, or any SEO / social-meta plugin.** Output tags from PHP / Blade.

## Every public template must output

| Tag | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| `<title>` | Prefer `{Page Title} \| Acreline`. Keep the visible title ≤ 60 characters — shorten the page title, not the brand, if it overflows. WordPress already prints `<title>` via `wp_head()`; set it with `document_title_parts` / `pre_get_document_title`, do not echo a second `<title>`. |
| `<meta name="description">` | 150–160 characters. Unique per template. |
| `<link rel="canonical">` | Absolute HTTPS URL of this view. |
| Open Graph | `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image`, `og:url`, `og:type` |
| Twitter | `twitter:card` = `summary_large_image`, plus `twitter:title`, `twitter:description` (and `twitter:image` when `og:image` exists) |

Also set `og:locale` / `og:site_name` when easy (`en_US`, `Acreline`).

## Where it lives

Put one native generator in the theme — prefer `App\Support\Seo` hooked from `app/setup.php` on `wp_head` (and title filters). Do **not** dump raw `echo` soup in `resources/views/layouts/app.blade.php` next to `@php(wp_head())`.

`layouts/app.blade.php` already calls `wp_head()`. Hook there. Escape everything (`esc_attr`, `esc_url`). Skip `is_admin()`, feeds, and REST.

## How to pick values

1. **Title** — page / listing / agent / post title. Front page: brand + short offer, not “Home | …”.
2. **Description** — `PageCopy` field if present (`hero_text`, excerpt), else listing `description`, else a general real-estate fallback. Never “luxury homes.” Concept voice: homes, neighborhoods, and local agents in a sample market. Mention fiction/sample only when the page is clearly demo chrome, not in every OG blurb.
3. **Canonical / og:url**
   - Front page: `home_url('/')`
   - Singular page, listing, agent, post: `get_permalink()`
   - Blog index: `get_permalink(get_option('page_for_posts'))` or `home_url('/blog/')`
   - Do not use `get_permalink()` on a non-singular query (it lies).
4. **Image** — featured image → listing `ks_image` → page `ks_hero_image` → a theme default under `public/` or the homepage Unsplash farmhouse. Absolute URL. `og:image` should be large (`summary_large_image`).
5. **og:type** — `website` on home/archives; `article` on posts; `og:type` `website` is fine for listings/agents unless you add RealEstate structured data separately.

JSON-LD already on the home template (`RealEstateAgent`) stays native in Blade. Do not add plugin schema. Keep `hello@acreline-concept.test` valid JSON (`@json(...)`), never `hello@@`.

## Do not

- Leave description as WordPress’s empty excerpt on marketing pages (they are field-driven).
- Output duplicate canonical / description if a tag already exists — one writer owns the head.
- Ship Rank Math / Yoast “just for now.” If a buyer later activates one, native tags must yield (see `marketplace.mdc` 8.2).
- Use the luxury-broker fallback from generic snippets. Default something like: `Sample homes and neighborhoods. Filter listings and book a fictional showing — Acreline concept demo.`

## When implementing

Add or extend `App\Support\Seo`. Wire it in `app/setup.php`. Afterward, curl a page and confirm title, description, canonical, `og:*`, and `twitter:*` are present once each.
